From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Barrios <25010449+nbarrios@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 22:02:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] crfpmoc: Support EC_CMD_FP_INFO v2/v3

Newer Zephyr FPMCU firmware (e.g. the USB srebrna FPMCU in the Lenovo
Googlebook 15) only implements FP_INFO v3 and answers v1 with
EC_RES_INVALID_VERSION. Query the supported versions with
EC_CMD_GET_CMD_VERSIONS v1 at open, use the highest of v3/v2/v1, size the
response for the header plus FP_MAX_CAPTURE_TYPES frame entries (the EC
refuses smaller buffers) and parse it into a version independent struct.
Frame parameters are informational only (the driver does not capture
images). Falls back to v1 if GET_CMD_VERSIONS fails.
